                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "RPG in which you play as Uther, an impoverished nobleman and thief, who explores dark medieval dungeons, engaging in turn-based combat and helping the inhabitants of a fictional German city\n\n✅Dungeons offer fights with various enemies, treasures, and traps\n✅Simple progression system\n✅The \"stealing from the rich to help the poor\" motif distinguishes the protagonist from standard heroes\n✅The music harmonizes well with the game's retro atmosphere\n✅Gradual experience gain and equipment upgrades provide the satisfaction of developing your party\n✅The visuals fit well with the style of classic RPGs\n\n❌The location layout is similar in many places\n❌The combat system doesn't introduce many new ideas and relies on familiar formulas\n❌The game world is small and limited primarily to a single settlement and the surrounding dungeons\n❌The price is too high\n\n✅✅ Verdict: [strike] Terrible [/strike], [strike] Bad [/strike], [strike] Mediocre [/strike], [b] Decent [/b], [strike] Good [/strike], [strike] Very Good [/strike] (Rating scale for short games, retro indie simulator games, and similar)\n\n[quote]If you'd like to see more of my reviews, you can find them on my\ncurator page:\n[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45994324/admin/reviews_manage/]CuratorKingViking[/url]\nand on my group:\n[url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/CuratorKingViking]GroupKingViking[/url]\n\nIf you have any questions about my reviews, feel free to ask.\nI'm happy to answer them. All reviews are my own!!\nBest regards, King Viking Bezimienny, Polish Game Reviewer. [/quote]",
